        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 84-year-old male patient, who presented with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he exhibited significant dyspnoea, increased sputum production, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without signs of pneumonia. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemic respiratory insufficiency. Blood tests showed mild systemic inflammation. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, resulting in satisfactory clinical improvement. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout the stay. The patient was discharged in stable condition with optimised inhaler therapy and a short course of oral steroids. Please ensure close follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
